module System/Memory

### One user at a time: `modifying g` waits until no other agent has `g` open, and it is used to read as well (an
### `Exclusive` `Guarded` has no `viewing`). The state is laid out as the runtime's ExclusiveAccess: free or taken,
### the agent holding it, and how often and how long agents waited for it. An agent that has to wait goes through the
### AccessManager, which stops the program when agents wait on each other (`[debug] deadlock-check`).
### :see: {AccessPolicy}, {MultiRead}, {Guarded}
record Exclusive
obeys AccessPolicy
    ### 0 free, 1 taken, 2 taken with an agent that may be waiting.
    secret state: U32
    ### The id of the agent holding it, 0 while free.
    secret holder: U64
    ### How many times an agent had to wait for it.
    secret waits: U64
    ### How long agents waited for it in all, in nanoseconds.
    secret waited: U64

### Creates a free exclusive access.
### :returns: The resulting `Exclusive` value.
routine Exclusive() -> Exclusive
    return Exclusive(state: 0, holder: 0, waits: 0, waited: 0)

### The AccessManager's kind for this policy: an exclusive access.
### :returns: 1.
@readonly
routine Exclusive.access_kind() -> U32
    return 1
